# Runtime state a copy produces: the object store's local root (objectstore.fs),
# created at the path the configuration names when the first object is written,
# and the token signing key the program generates on its first run. Both belong
# to a deployment and not to the source tree.
/var/

# The frontend's build outputs, which no checkout commits: the installed
# dependency tree and the built bundle. web/dist is a build output but has to
# hold at least one file for go:embed to compile (the Go program embeds
# web/dist), so web/dist/index.html is committed as a placeholder -- tracked
# despite this rule, kept in step by force-adding it when it changes. A real
# build replaces its contents in place. See web/README.md.
/web/node_modules/
/web/dist/
